   "source": [
    "#### 1. Search"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "4a4ceff8-8764-4d2b-9fe2-18ee7ae6082f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Example: Navigation; logistics;\n",
    "Maps suggest the best possible route using algorithms:Optimization\n",
    "Delivery charges based on distance, availability of agents\n",
    "Search problems: \n",
    "1. Agent: entitiy that learn the environment and acts upon tha environment; Example: Driver in a car\n",
    "2. State: Configuration of the agent and its environment; Eg: different places on the route that we would encounter while travel\n",
    "3. Initial State: The state in which the agent begins; Eg: Source \n",
    "4. Actions: Choices that can be executed in a particular state Eg: The directions we chose\n",
    "5. Transition model: ----\n",
    "6. State space: All the possible states which is reachable from source\n",
    "7. Goal test/ Destination test: Ways to determin whether a given state is a goal state\n",
    "8. Path cost: Numerical cost associated with a given path\n",
    "----\n",
    "9. Optimal solution\n",
    "10. Node: Data structure that keeps track of : state/parent(node that generated this node)/action/path cost\n",
    "11. Approach: \n",
    "Depth First Search\n",
    "- May not deliver solution if takes wrong route\n",
    "Breadth first search: Search that always expands the shallowest node in the frontier\n",
    "+ Guarantees the solution\n",
    "Uninformed Search: No specific knowledge\n",
    "Informed search: uses problem specific knowledge to find the solutions more efficiently\n",
    "-> Greedy Best-First Search: Heuristic decisions\n",
    "- Won't know where is the dead end"
   ]
  }
 ],
